<title>USA: General Motors unit may issue $500 mln notes.</title>
<headline>General Motors unit may issue $500 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Acceptance Corp, a unit of General Motors Corp, is expected to issue $500 million in four-year notes on Monday via Lehman Brothers, according to market sources.</p>
<p>General Motors Acceptance Corp is a finance arm of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>The A3/A- issue is expected to be non-callable and has price talk at around 40 basis point over the 6-1/2 percent U.S. Treasury note due May 2001, market sources added.</p>
<p>((- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 -)</p>
